 "capsule": "Qin (秦) was a Zhou-era state in the Wei River valley of modern Shaanxi, traditionally enfeoffed in 897 BCE and long regarded by the central Chinese states as a semi-barbarian frontier power. Sweeping Legalist reforms under Lord Shang in the 4th century BCE built a centralized bureaucratic and military machine that let Qin conquer the other six major Warring States one by one. Its king Ying Zheng completed unification in 221 BCE and took the title First Emperor, founding the short-lived Qin dynasty.",
